  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Lavender oil, an essential oil distilled from lavender flowers, is used as an anxiolytic, that is, to relieve anxiety. It is classified as an approved herbal medicinal product and is used as an other anxiolytic within the nervous system drug class, though it is not an EU-wide centrally authorised medicine.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q900534&quot;>Wikidata Q900534</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>Lavandulae aetheroleum</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>N05BX05</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB14566&quot;>DB14566</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q900534&quot;>Q900534</a></td></tr></table></body></html>"));
